<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rufisque</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rufisque is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cap-vert">Cap-Vert</a> peninsula east of Dakar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a>. A Portuguese and then French trading post, it became the main port for groundnut exports in the late 19th century and in 1880 one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/four-communes">Four Communes</a>, whose inhabitants held French citizenship. It has since been absorbed into the Dakar metropolitan area.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rufisque.jpg" alt="Rufisque" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Myriam Louviot (MyriamLouviot) · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RufisqueQuincaillerie.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
